WEBVTT

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:10.375
Holding course 351 mark 10.
Warp 7.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:13.402
We'll be passing a red dwarf
system in 40 minutes.

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.744
I can't tell yet if there
are any M-Class planets.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:20.945
You ready?

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:21.976
No, I really want

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:23.716
to get on that transtator
assembly diagnostic.

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:26.851
Harry, I can't do this alone.

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:28.190
Sorry.

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:30.594
Oh, you're making a big mistake.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.291
Can't you see
what's going to happen?

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:38.635
We're the only humans
out here, Harry.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:41.003
People are going
to start pairing off

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:42.770
and if we don't get
to the Delaney sisters

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.800
in Stellar Cartography soon,
somebody else will.

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:46.812
I got a girl back home.

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:48.211
So what?
I got five.

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:50.808
I plan on seeing mine again.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.683
Harry, Harry, Harry,
Harry, Harry.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.449
You really think
she's going to wait for you?

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:56.614
I hope so.

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:58.283
Let her go.

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:01.293
Let her have a husband
and kids and a good life,

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:03.352
while you and I have
the Delaney sisters.

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:06.957
I told you, I need to run
a transtator diagnostic.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.661
You need to run
a self-diagnostic.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.692
Look, they come as a pair.

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:13.069
It's a double date or no date.

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:15.631
Come on.

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:17.575
I told them all about you.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.078
What did you tell them
about me?

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:22.377
Oh, well, for one thing,

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:24.940
how you broke
the single-pilot speed record

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:26.076
at the Academy.

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:27.711
Record?

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:29.585
I never broke any record.

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:31.715
And who are they going
to check it with?

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:38.631
Report!

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:40.098
We're at the leading edge
of a shock wave.

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:59.211
Minor hull breach on Deck 3,
contained.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.879
Shields are holding.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.888
Engineering is undamaged,
Captain.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:04.549
All systems operational.

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:09.625
Mr. Paris, can you identify
the source of the wave?

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:12.096
I'm not sure.

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:14.225
Scanners are picking
up a debris cloud

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.667
in the red dwarf system
we're approaching.

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:19.069
It consists of differentially
charged polaric ions,

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:20.197
Captain.

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:24.810
Differentially charged?

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:28.177
That would suggest
a massive detonation.

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:30.876
Are you familiar
with any intelligent life-forms

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:32.441
in this system, Mr. Neelix?

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:33.975
Familiar?

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:36.715
Ah, not exactly, uh, "familiar."

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:39.691
Considerably less
than "familiar," actually.

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:43.762
Adjust course to investigate.

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:44.785
Aye, Captain.

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:53.401
Entering the system, Captain.

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:55.669
Heading 010 mark 4.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:56.732
Kes...

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:58.801
what are you doing here?

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:00.813
I had to know.

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:03.315
Know? Know what?

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:05.544
The origin of the shock wave
is an M-Class planet, Captain.

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:06.813
We're within visual range.

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:07.979
On screen.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:13.051
All vegetation on the planet
has been destroyed.

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:14.354
No satellite system in orbit.

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:15.520
No evidence of spacecraft.

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:16.859
Life signs?

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:18.295
- None.
- None.

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:19.696
But the polaric radiation

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:21.461
may be interfering
with the scanners.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:22.968
Take us into orbit.

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:25.664
Density patterns on the surface
show artificial waterways

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:27.434
and a global aqueduct system.

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:31.239
There is a civilization
down there, Captain.

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:33.643
Or there was.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.580
What do we know
about surface conditions?

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:37.776
Radiation is within
acceptable levels.

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:39.444
Atmosphere: Breathable.

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:42.079
Mr. Paris, Tuvok,
you're with me.

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:43.645
Ms. Torres, meet us
in Transporter Room 2.

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:44.657
On my way.

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:46.556
Commander, you have the Bridge.

00:06:17.976 --> 00:06:21.673
The entire surface of the planet
was just... seared.

00:06:21.713 --> 00:06:24.876
There was a chain reaction
in subspace,

00:06:24.916 --> 00:06:26.850
very likely ignited
by the detonation

00:06:26.885 --> 00:06:29.183
of one or more
polaric ion devices.

00:06:29.221 --> 00:06:30.813
If that's what happened,

00:06:30.856 --> 00:06:32.653
the people here
never had a chance.

00:06:32.691 --> 00:06:35.524
They're gone... vaporized.

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:38.051
Everything organic
has basically been obliterated.

00:06:38.096 --> 00:06:39.757
At least it happened quickly.

00:06:39.798 --> 00:06:40.958
Polaric detonation

00:06:41.066 --> 00:06:43.227
would have swept through
this city in seconds.

00:06:43.268 --> 00:06:45.259
It recalls
the Chaltok IV incident.

00:06:45.303 --> 00:06:46.770
Chaltok IV?

00:06:46.805 --> 00:06:48.796
A Romulan research colony
was nearly destroyed

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:50.808
during a testing
of one of these devices.

00:06:50.842 --> 00:06:54.243
It led to the Polaric
Test Ban Treaty of 2268.

00:06:54.279 --> 00:06:58.909
So... we're looking
at the end of a war.

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:01.578
I wonder who won.

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:03.713
I'm not so sure there was a war.

00:07:03.755 --> 00:07:05.586
Look at these readings,
B'Elanna.

00:07:10.228 --> 00:07:12.253
Polaric ion concentrations

00:07:12.297 --> 00:07:15.494
are so high, I can't get
an accurate reading.

00:07:15.534 --> 00:07:17.434
I'd say these conduits
were the source

00:07:17.469 --> 00:07:18.731
of the explosion, wouldn't you?

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:22.035
A civilization powered
by polaric ion energy?

00:07:23.074 --> 00:07:25.065
That's what it looks like.

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:27.704
A time bomb
underneath every street,

00:07:27.746 --> 00:07:29.805
running into every home.

00:07:33.552 --> 00:07:36.043
What do you mean, you saw it?

00:07:36.087 --> 00:07:37.782
How could you see it?

00:07:37.823 --> 00:07:39.586
I don't know.

00:07:43.028 --> 00:07:44.552
What did you see?

00:07:47.833 --> 00:07:49.528
I saw them...

00:07:52.003 --> 00:07:53.265
burn...

00:07:55.774 --> 00:07:57.503
their bodies...

00:08:00.412 --> 00:08:02.676
ashes where they stood!

00:08:06.451 --> 00:08:08.885
You felt the shock wave
in your sleep.

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:11.252
This is just your imagination.

00:08:11.289 --> 00:08:14.053
A strange coincidence.

00:08:14.092 --> 00:08:15.389
I don't think so.

00:08:15.427 --> 00:08:17.019
What else could it be?

00:08:17.062 --> 00:08:19.257
It was...

00:08:19.297 --> 00:08:22.198
it was almost telepathic.

00:08:22.234 --> 00:08:27.536
Telepathy is a message,
words, a voice...

00:08:27.572 --> 00:08:32.066
What you're describing,
why, it's... almost like

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:34.374
the visions of Drakina
Forest dwellers.

00:08:34.412 --> 00:08:36.403
Who?

00:08:36.448 --> 00:08:38.939
A tribe
with paranormal abilities.

00:08:39.017 --> 00:08:40.484
They can walk
into an empty room...

00:08:40.519 --> 00:08:44.353
Neelix, my ancestors
were said to have

00:08:44.389 --> 00:08:47.517
unusual mental abilities.

00:08:48.894 --> 00:08:51.260
No one believes those stories.

00:08:51.296 --> 00:08:53.958
I always have.

00:09:23.161 --> 00:09:24.628
Look.

00:09:24.663 --> 00:09:27.131
This may be some kind
of timepiece

00:09:27.165 --> 00:09:30.157
stopped at the moment
of the explosion.

00:09:35.974 --> 00:09:37.134
What was that?

00:09:37.175 --> 00:09:38.164
What?

00:09:39.177 --> 00:09:40.838
Didn't you hear that?

00:09:40.879 --> 00:09:43.370
Hear what, Lieutenant?

00:09:43.415 --> 00:09:44.939
Kids playing.

00:09:45.050 --> 00:09:46.210
They were as close to me as...

00:10:05.236 --> 00:10:07.397
I don't understand.

00:10:07.439 --> 00:10:11.876
I was here, in this square,
but there were people.

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:13.844
You never left here, Tom.

00:10:13.878 --> 00:10:15.140
But I saw them.

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:17.444
Lots of people.

00:10:17.482 --> 00:10:18.881
Children playing

00:10:18.917 --> 00:10:19.975
and the sun was shining.

00:10:20.018 --> 00:10:22.111
There was no evidence
of an explosion.

00:10:22.153 --> 00:10:23.950
Everyone was alive and happy.

00:10:23.989 --> 00:10:25.980
You were standing here
the whole time.

00:10:26.091 --> 00:10:28.719
Your central nervous system
is showing a temporal flux,

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:30.751
but it's rapidly
returning to normal.

00:10:30.795 --> 00:10:32.922
The chain reaction has
shattered subspace, Captain.

00:10:32.964 --> 00:10:35.455
I want everyone to stand
exactly where they are.

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:37.991
If Tuvok's right,
there may be subspace fractures

00:10:38.036 --> 00:10:41.005
floating like icebergs
across the planet's surface.

00:10:41.039 --> 00:10:42.370
Away team to Voyager.

00:10:42.407 --> 00:10:43.374
Go ahead.

00:10:43.408 --> 00:10:44.432
Four to beam up.

00:10:49.147 --> 00:10:51.115
Tuvok, B'Elanna?

00:10:56.588 --> 00:10:58.283
Hey, calm down.

00:10:58.323 --> 00:10:59.790
It's all right.

00:10:59.824 --> 00:11:01.451
Now what's the problem?

00:11:01.493 --> 00:11:02.824
I saw them!

00:11:02.861 --> 00:11:04.590
They appeared out of thin air!

00:11:04.629 --> 00:11:07.530
They're some kind of demons.

00:11:07.565 --> 00:11:09.362
I saw them with my own eyes.

00:11:09.401 --> 00:11:10.595
I'm sorry we startled him.

00:11:10.635 --> 00:11:11.795
We just came around the corner.

00:11:11.836 --> 00:11:13.463
They're lying!

00:11:13.505 --> 00:11:14.665
Shh, now.

00:11:14.706 --> 00:11:16.606
Calm down.
You've been reading

00:11:16.641 --> 00:11:18.871
too many of those Darkstorm
tales, young fellow.

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:21.242
There's no such thing as demons.

00:11:21.279 --> 00:11:22.303
But I'm telling you...

00:11:22.347 --> 00:11:24.372
Ah, ah, ah, run along now.

00:11:24.416 --> 00:11:27.351
Have a confection bar
and calm down.

00:11:27.385 --> 00:11:31.185
All right, everybody,
back to your business.

00:11:31.222 --> 00:11:32.883
Nothing else to see here now.

00:11:34.693 --> 00:11:36.456
Oh, sorry about that.

00:11:36.494 --> 00:11:37.688
No problem.

00:11:37.729 --> 00:11:39.959
Who knows what gets
into their heads, huh?

00:11:39.998 --> 00:11:42.193
Oh, perhaps the
uniforms scared him.

00:11:42.233 --> 00:11:43.632
We're not from this area.

00:11:43.668 --> 00:11:45.499
Come in on
the Continental Transport?

00:11:45.537 --> 00:11:46.504
This morning.

00:11:46.538 --> 00:11:48.699
Is, uh, that
what they're wearing

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:50.367
in Kalto province these days?

00:11:50.408 --> 00:11:53.707
Uh, this is, uh, a little
more formal than most.

00:11:53.745 --> 00:11:55.337
You know how it is
when you travel.

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:57.109
We were actually looking
for a clothing shop.

00:11:57.148 --> 00:12:00.379
We thought we'd change
into something more appropriate.

00:12:00.418 --> 00:12:01.578
There's one right over there.

00:12:01.619 --> 00:12:03.678
I hope the rest of your stay
with us is more enjoyable.

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:07.620
I wish I could say it will be.

00:12:16.434 --> 00:12:18.402
Need a timepiece?

00:12:19.771 --> 00:12:21.204
Maybe you could help me.

00:12:21.239 --> 00:12:23.867
I'm from... Kalto province.

00:12:23.908 --> 00:12:25.967
I'm not used to your timepieces.

00:12:26.044 --> 00:12:28.410
They're no different
than Kalton timepieces.

00:12:28.446 --> 00:12:31.938
Are you sure?
What do these numbers stand for?

00:12:31.983 --> 00:12:34.884
Rotations, intervals, fractions.

00:12:34.919 --> 00:12:36.580
Same as any timepiece.

00:12:36.621 --> 00:12:37.986
14 kelodas.

00:12:38.056 --> 00:12:41.253
A fair price.

00:12:41.292 --> 00:12:43.157
I might stop back later.

00:12:43.194 --> 00:12:44.354
If there's time.

00:12:46.998 --> 00:12:48.659
If I understood correctly,

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:51.601
this world is going to be
destroyed sometime tomorrow.

00:12:59.043 --> 00:13:01.011
First Officer's Log,
supplemental.

00:13:01.045 --> 00:13:03.946
There's been no sign of Captain
Janeway or Lieutenant Paris

00:13:03.982 --> 00:13:06.542
since they were lost
in a subspace fracture.

00:13:06.584 --> 00:13:08.711
This is one of the subspace
fractures we've located

00:13:08.753 --> 00:13:10.744
with a magneton
scan of the surface.

00:13:10.789 --> 00:13:12.552
This is the time
of the explosion

00:13:12.590 --> 00:13:13.921
where the fracture opens.

00:13:13.958 --> 00:13:15.949
The, as the shock waves
dissipate,

00:13:15.994 --> 00:13:17.859
the fracture grows more narrow.

00:13:17.896 --> 00:13:20.421
We believe that the Captain
and Lieutenant Paris

00:13:20.465 --> 00:13:21.955
are trapped at the narrow end.

00:13:22.033 --> 00:13:24.126
Shock waves from most explosions
dissipate

00:13:24.169 --> 00:13:27.071
into the future, but we're
speculating... based in part

00:13:27.204 --> 00:13:28.671
on what Paris told us he saw...

00:13:28.705 --> 00:13:31.105
that these dissipate
into the past.

00:13:31.141 --> 00:13:32.108
That's consistent

00:13:32.142 --> 00:13:33.905
with the subspace damage
we've observed.

00:13:33.944 --> 00:13:35.571
Why haven't they
been able to return

00:13:35.612 --> 00:13:37.307
as Mr. Paris did the first time?

00:13:37.347 --> 00:13:40.510
He wasn't all the way
inside a fracture.

00:13:40.551 --> 00:13:42.246
Remember? We still saw Paris
standing there

00:13:42.286 --> 00:13:43.981
even when he could see
the other side.

00:13:44.021 --> 00:13:46.649
So it's possible the Captain
and Paris are existing

00:13:46.690 --> 00:13:49.124
only hours and minutes
before the explosion occurs.

00:13:49.159 --> 00:13:51.525
There's no way for us to measure

00:13:51.562 --> 00:13:54.395
exactly how far back
these fractures go.

00:13:54.431 --> 00:13:56.160
How do we find them?

00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:58.100
If I know Captain Janeway,

00:13:58.135 --> 00:14:00.968
she would activate
a subspace beacon to assist us.

00:14:01.004 --> 00:14:02.369
We're counting on it.

00:14:02.406 --> 00:14:03.873
First, we have to find
a fracture

00:14:03.907 --> 00:14:05.374
in a location where they've been

00:14:05.409 --> 00:14:07.604
then we have to microscan
the fracture

00:14:07.644 --> 00:14:09.908
to try to pick up the signal
from their subspace beacon.

00:14:09.947 --> 00:14:12.916
Once we've identified
where and when they are,

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:15.646
then we have to widen
the fracture at that point.

00:14:15.686 --> 00:14:17.847
How do you suggest we do that?

00:14:19.556 --> 00:14:21.421
We're not sure yet.

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:30.762
Hmm.

00:14:34.138 --> 00:14:35.696
Mm-hmm.

00:14:35.739 --> 00:14:37.229
- What?
- Hmm?

00:14:37.274 --> 00:14:38.434
Is something wrong?

00:14:38.475 --> 00:14:39.567
Yes, terribly wrong.

00:14:39.610 --> 00:14:42.773
Your brain is... not on file.

00:14:42.813 --> 00:14:44.974
Either your government
failed to transmit

00:14:45.048 --> 00:14:47.744
the standard 15-501
Crew Personnel Report

00:14:47.784 --> 00:14:50.753
or somebody at Starfleet Medical
really fouled up.

00:14:50.787 --> 00:14:52.982
I'm not a member
of the Starfleet crew.

00:14:53.056 --> 00:14:55.217
We came aboard
at mid-expedition.

00:14:55.259 --> 00:14:56.248
And no one asked you

00:14:56.293 --> 00:14:58.454
for your medical histories
when you arrived?

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:03.527
Of course not... that would be
the ship's doctor's job.

00:15:03.567 --> 00:15:05.159
My job.

00:15:05.202 --> 00:15:08.763
If anyone had bothered
to tell me about new passengers,

00:15:08.805 --> 00:15:10.363
but I seem to be
the last to know

00:15:10.407 --> 00:15:12.272
just about everything
around here.

00:15:12.309 --> 00:15:14.436
So. Tell me...

00:15:14.478 --> 00:15:17.709
just how many other
new arrivals are there?

00:15:17.748 --> 00:15:18.840
Just us.

00:15:18.882 --> 00:15:20.440
And the crew from another ship
that was destroyed.

00:15:20.484 --> 00:15:22.884
Another... crew?

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:25.047
That's nice.

00:15:25.088 --> 00:15:28.546
This is the emergency
medical holographic system

00:15:28.592 --> 00:15:30.082
to Captain Janeway.

00:15:30.127 --> 00:15:31.253
She's not on board.

00:15:31.295 --> 00:15:33.320
She's missing
on the surface of a planet.

00:15:34.364 --> 00:15:35.490
Missing?

00:15:35.532 --> 00:15:38.695
The Captain is missing?

00:15:41.071 --> 00:15:44.336
It seems I've found myself
on the voyage of the damned.

00:15:44.374 --> 00:15:46.934
Very well.

00:15:46.977 --> 00:15:48.911
Please advise
the highest-ranking officer

00:15:48.946 --> 00:15:51.107
who is not missing

00:15:51.148 --> 00:15:54.413
to see me
at his earliest convenience.

00:15:54.451 --> 00:15:55.645
You may shut off my program now.

00:15:55.686 --> 00:15:58.814
But you haven't told us anything
about her condition.

00:15:58.855 --> 00:16:01.449
She's the healthiest member
of her species I've ever seen...

00:16:01.491 --> 00:16:04.654
the only member of her species
I've ever seen.

00:16:04.695 --> 00:16:07.789
You have a lovely brain.

00:16:07.831 --> 00:16:10.391
It will make a fine
addition to our files.

00:16:11.401 --> 00:16:12.561
I wouldn't worry.

00:16:12.603 --> 00:16:14.036
If your species has a history

00:16:14.071 --> 00:16:15.732
of extraordinary
mental abilities,

00:16:15.772 --> 00:16:18.400
this may simply be your way
of flexing those muscles

00:16:18.442 --> 00:16:19.773
for the first time.

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:22.278
Living in space requires
the body to make

00:16:22.312 --> 00:16:23.677
a variety of biological
adjustments.

00:16:23.714 --> 00:16:26.945
This could be a side effect
of that process.

00:16:26.984 --> 00:16:28.349
Go home.

00:16:28.385 --> 00:16:32.287
Get a good night's sleep...
and drink plenty of fluids.

00:16:32.322 --> 00:16:33.653
Fluids?

00:16:33.690 --> 00:16:35.885
Everybody should drink
plenty of fluids.

00:16:35.926 --> 00:16:37.894
Don't leave
without turning me off.

00:16:37.928 --> 00:16:39.759
Computer, end program.

00:16:39.796 --> 00:16:40.922
And call me in the morning.

00:16:47.971 --> 00:16:49.165
We can assume that Voyager

00:16:49.206 --> 00:16:50.935
will be looking for a way
to reach us.

00:16:50.974 --> 00:16:53.772
I'll set my combadge
to emit a subspace beacon.

00:16:53.810 --> 00:16:55.437
If they get close,
maybe they'll pick it up.

00:16:56.546 --> 00:16:58.070
I know.

00:16:58.115 --> 00:16:59.275
Maybe there's some way...

00:16:59.316 --> 00:17:01.045
Don't even think about it, Tom.

00:17:01.084 --> 00:17:02.779
The Prime Directive is clear.

00:17:02.819 --> 00:17:04.013
We cannot allow our presence

00:17:04.054 --> 00:17:06.079
to alter this planet's
natural course of events.

00:17:06.123 --> 00:17:08.455
Even if the natural course
of events is annihilation?

00:17:08.492 --> 00:17:09.550
Yeah.

00:17:09.593 --> 00:17:12.255
My father used
to talk at length to us

00:17:12.296 --> 00:17:13.263
about the Prime Directive,

00:17:13.297 --> 00:17:14.924
once a year...
like a holiday sermon.

00:17:14.998 --> 00:17:16.590
He considered it
the guiding principle

00:17:16.633 --> 00:17:17.930
of space exploration.

00:17:18.001 --> 00:17:18.933
To be honest,

00:17:19.002 --> 00:17:22.165
I tuned out most of his sermons
years ago.

00:17:22.205 --> 00:17:24.696
Well, tune back into this one
because I agree with him.

00:17:24.741 --> 00:17:26.675
You have no idea
what the consequences might be

00:17:26.710 --> 00:17:28.143
once you involve yourself.

00:17:28.178 --> 00:17:31.341
The consequences would have to
be better than mass destruction.

00:17:31.381 --> 00:17:33.474
You're not to warn these people.

00:17:33.517 --> 00:17:34.984
That's an order.

00:17:38.288 --> 00:17:39.516
Oh, God. Come on.

00:17:44.361 --> 00:17:45.885
I know you're lying.

00:17:45.929 --> 00:17:48.159
Young man, we're here
on a business trip

00:17:48.198 --> 00:17:49.961
and we have a lot of work to do.

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:51.092
The Officer told me

00:17:51.134 --> 00:17:53.500
you came here
on the Continental Transport.

00:17:53.537 --> 00:17:55.801
That's right.
We're from Kalto province.

00:17:55.839 --> 00:17:58.433
Yeah? Well, I just talked
to the transport attendant.

00:17:58.475 --> 00:18:01.205
He told me four people
came today from Kalto.

00:18:01.244 --> 00:18:03.439
Two of them were
a lot older than you

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:05.380
and they had a child with them.

00:18:05.415 --> 00:18:06.848
Well, the attendant was wrong.

00:18:06.883 --> 00:18:08.316
That was us.

00:18:08.352 --> 00:18:10.149
So, where's the child?

00:18:10.187 --> 00:18:12.052
We ate him.

00:18:12.089 --> 00:18:14.853
Because we are demons
and we eat children.

00:18:14.891 --> 00:18:17.086
And I haven't had my supper yet.

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:26.333
Sorry, I just figured
it was the quickest way.

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:28.201
Let's concentrate
on getting out of here.

00:18:35.879 --> 00:18:39.042
The same subspace fractures
that brought us here

00:18:39.082 --> 00:18:40.572
might still be around.

00:18:40.617 --> 00:18:44.451
If they were caused
by a polaric explosion

00:18:44.488 --> 00:18:47.855
is there any way we could use
polaric energy to get us back?

00:18:51.528 --> 00:18:54.588
If we had access to
a polaric ion generator,

00:18:54.631 --> 00:18:57.361
we could modify a tricorder
to emit a polaric field.

00:18:57.401 --> 00:18:59.801
At the very least, it might
help us scan for a fracture.

00:19:01.037 --> 00:19:03.267
I wonder where these
conduits get their power.

00:19:10.247 --> 00:19:12.408
This is a lawful demonstration.

00:19:12.449 --> 00:19:14.542
We have a right to be here!

00:19:17.454 --> 00:19:19.718
Under normal circumstances,

00:19:19.756 --> 00:19:21.690
I'd say we should
come back tomorrow.

00:19:52.722 --> 00:19:55.088
This device uses
the same polaric energy

00:19:55.125 --> 00:19:56.456
that destroyed the planet.

00:19:56.493 --> 00:19:59.291
At intense levels,
it can open a subspace fracture.

00:19:59.329 --> 00:20:01.729
Wide enough for the Captain
and Paris to get through?

00:20:01.765 --> 00:20:03.232
If we can locate them,

00:20:03.266 --> 00:20:05.097
this is capable
of bringing them back.

00:20:05.135 --> 00:20:06.568
The logical place
to begin would be

00:20:06.603 --> 00:20:08.230
at the same location
they disappeared.

00:20:10.173 --> 00:20:12.733
The only problem is,
at the necessary intensity,

00:20:12.776 --> 00:20:14.710
the polaric generator
will burn itself out

00:20:14.744 --> 00:20:16.473
after 30 seconds at best.

00:20:16.513 --> 00:20:18.845
Can't we reinitialize the
generator and try again?

00:20:18.882 --> 00:20:20.645
Not at the same location.

00:20:20.684 --> 00:20:23.209
Once we make an attempt
at any given location,

00:20:23.253 --> 00:20:24.686
the damage to subspace

00:20:24.721 --> 00:20:26.382
will make a second attempt
impossible.

00:20:26.423 --> 00:20:29.221
How do we prevent one of us from
getting trapped in a fracture?

00:20:29.259 --> 00:20:32.524
We've modified our tricorders
to detect the fractures

00:20:32.562 --> 00:20:34.860
and all of us will be
wearing one of these.

00:20:34.898 --> 00:20:36.866
It puts out
an anti-polaric field.

00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:38.561
It should repel the fractures

00:20:38.602 --> 00:20:40.229
when they get
within three meters.

00:20:40.270 --> 00:20:41.635
Nice work.

00:20:42.906 --> 00:20:44.271
Ah, Commander.

00:20:46.610 --> 00:20:49.101
Will you be going back
to the planet's surface?

00:20:49.145 --> 00:20:50.544
We're getting ready
to leave right now.

00:20:50.580 --> 00:20:51.877
I have to go with you.

00:20:51.915 --> 00:20:54.748
There's nothing down there
you want to see, Kes.

00:20:54.784 --> 00:20:56.115
That's what I told her.

00:20:56.152 --> 00:20:58.416
I've already seen it.
I have to go.

00:21:10.300 --> 00:21:12.632
We're sorry
to involve you in this.

00:21:12.669 --> 00:21:14.637
Pe'Nar Makull.

00:21:14.671 --> 00:21:16.662
My colleague, Ny Terla.

00:21:16.706 --> 00:21:18.571
Apparently, you just
happened to be

00:21:18.608 --> 00:21:20.872
at the wrong place
at the wrong time.

00:21:20.911 --> 00:21:23.106
I was just thinking
the very same thing.

00:21:23.146 --> 00:21:25.137
What were you doing there?

00:21:25.181 --> 00:21:26.808
We're from Kalto province.

00:21:26.850 --> 00:21:30.387
We were hoping to tour
your power facility...

00:21:30.520 --> 00:21:31.418
compare it to our own.

00:21:31.454 --> 00:21:33.979
I've never seen a Kalton
with your color hair.

00:21:34.090 --> 00:21:37.150
Well, now you have.

00:21:37.193 --> 00:21:39.388
My friend thinks you were sent

00:21:39.429 --> 00:21:41.090
by the government
to infiltrate us.

00:21:41.131 --> 00:21:42.894
Infiltrate?

00:21:42.932 --> 00:21:45.230
You were there
when she got this.

00:21:45.268 --> 00:21:47.998
Perhaps you were told
to put on a good show for us.

00:21:48.037 --> 00:21:50.665
We don't even know why someone
would want to infiltrate you.

00:21:52.041 --> 00:21:53.872
That's hard to believe.

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:57.004
Even in Kalto, there are
protests against polaric energy.

00:21:57.113 --> 00:21:58.580
We're not spies.

00:21:58.615 --> 00:22:01.379
When was the last time
you were in a power plant?

00:22:01.418 --> 00:22:02.942
Not since we left home.

00:22:03.019 --> 00:22:04.884
You weren't
in that plant yesterday?

00:22:04.921 --> 00:22:08.789
We were just getting there
when we stumbled into you.

00:22:09.859 --> 00:22:12.089
We know you're not
telling the truth.

00:22:12.128 --> 00:22:15.529
We have safety monitors
to measure polaric energy.

00:22:15.565 --> 00:22:17.692
When you were brought here,

00:22:17.734 --> 00:22:20.965
they registered five times
the normal readings.

00:22:22.839 --> 00:22:24.136
To register levels this high,

00:22:24.174 --> 00:22:27.143
you were either inside
that plant yesterday

00:22:27.177 --> 00:22:28.576
or...

00:22:28.611 --> 00:22:30.636
at the site
of a polaric disaster

00:22:30.680 --> 00:22:33.240
worse than any in the history
of this planet.

00:22:57.907 --> 00:23:00.102
What is it?

00:23:00.143 --> 00:23:04.477
It's as though I can sense
the people who were here.

00:23:04.514 --> 00:23:07.039
I know.

00:23:07.083 --> 00:23:09.643
It's like walking
through a graveyard.

00:23:09.686 --> 00:23:11.085
No.

00:23:11.120 --> 00:23:13.315
It's more than that.

00:23:13.356 --> 00:23:17.258
I almost feel...

00:23:17.293 --> 00:23:20.854
as if I could touch
the people who were here.

00:23:28.638 --> 00:23:30.538
What have you found?

00:23:30.573 --> 00:23:32.768
The scanners are not showing
any subspace fractures

00:23:32.809 --> 00:23:34.401
in the area now.

00:23:34.444 --> 00:23:36.503
That probably indicates
the subspace damage

00:23:36.546 --> 00:23:37.979
is beginning to dissipate.

00:23:38.081 --> 00:23:40.276
If that's true,
it's going to be harder

00:23:40.316 --> 00:23:42.580
to locate Tom and the Captain.

00:23:42.619 --> 00:23:44.314
Commander, I'm picking up
a signal from a combadge.

00:23:44.354 --> 00:23:45.981
The subspace beacon?

00:23:46.022 --> 00:23:48.320
No, it's not on subspace.

00:23:48.358 --> 00:23:50.724
It's here... now.

00:23:52.195 --> 00:23:53.492
Kim to Janeway.

00:23:54.831 --> 00:23:55.991
Kim to Paris.

00:23:56.065 --> 00:23:58.727
Can we locate
the source of the signal?

00:23:58.768 --> 00:24:00.326
Yes, sir.

00:24:00.370 --> 00:24:01.894
This way.

00:24:05.842 --> 00:24:07.275
What's your name?

00:24:07.310 --> 00:24:08.470
Janeway.

00:24:08.511 --> 00:24:09.773
Unusual name.

00:24:09.812 --> 00:24:11.336
Not where I'm from.

00:24:11.381 --> 00:24:13.713
What part of Kalto province
was that again?

00:24:13.750 --> 00:24:15.411
I don't see any point in this.

00:24:15.451 --> 00:24:17.942
There is a point,
a very important one.

00:24:18.054 --> 00:24:19.783
It has to do with our schedule

00:24:19.822 --> 00:24:22.382
and whether we
can keep it or not.

00:24:23.459 --> 00:24:24.426
Can we?

00:24:24.460 --> 00:24:26.587
I don't know.

00:24:27.997 --> 00:24:29.692
Do they know our plan?

00:24:29.732 --> 00:24:31.859
I have no idea.

00:24:31.901 --> 00:24:33.163
Let me go!

00:24:33.202 --> 00:24:36.899
Look what I caught
sneaking around outside.

00:24:50.086 --> 00:24:51.781
I'm still not showing
any life signs.

00:25:02.465 --> 00:25:04.365
The boy has nothing
to do with any of this.

00:25:04.400 --> 00:25:05.697
Is he yours?

00:25:05.735 --> 00:25:07.896
No. He's just somebody
we met here.

00:25:07.937 --> 00:25:08.904
Don't trust them.

00:25:08.938 --> 00:25:10.200
They aren't
who they say they are.

00:25:10.239 --> 00:25:11.706
Really?

00:25:11.741 --> 00:25:13.436
Thanks, kid.

00:25:13.476 --> 00:25:15.944
Look, this is all
a misunderstanding.

00:25:16.045 --> 00:25:17.535
They lied about coming here

00:25:17.580 --> 00:25:18.945
on the
Continental Transport.

00:25:18.982 --> 00:25:21.212
I talked
to the attendant myself.

00:25:21.250 --> 00:25:22.239
Let me go...

00:25:22.285 --> 00:25:23.718
What do we do with him?

00:25:23.753 --> 00:25:25.084
We can't let him go.

00:25:26.756 --> 00:25:29.884
Just put him over there
with the other.

00:25:33.596 --> 00:25:35.996
Now stay quiet.

00:25:52.582 --> 00:25:53.981
The combadge is designed
to self-activate

00:25:54.083 --> 00:25:55.983
when the casing is destroyed.

00:25:56.019 --> 00:25:58.681
To help searchers
locate victims.

00:26:02.191 --> 00:26:03.158
I guess it means

00:26:03.192 --> 00:26:05.126
they were caught
in the explosion.

00:26:05.161 --> 00:26:08.619
It only means their combadges
were caught in the explosion.

00:26:08.665 --> 00:26:11.156
Further speculation
serves no purpose.

00:26:11.200 --> 00:26:13.828
I suggest we search
for other tangible evidence.

00:26:22.478 --> 00:26:25.038
None of us have seen devices
like these before.

00:26:25.081 --> 00:26:27.572
Terla believes
they're spy equipment.

00:26:28.851 --> 00:26:30.944
They're for surveying property.

00:26:31.054 --> 00:26:33.113
I've been thinking
of buying land here.

00:26:33.156 --> 00:26:34.487
I need to survey it.

00:26:34.524 --> 00:26:36.515
I'd be curious
to know how they work.

00:26:36.559 --> 00:26:38.550
Would you show me?

00:26:43.032 --> 00:26:45.728
But then one of them
might be a weapon.

00:26:45.768 --> 00:26:47.292
And I wouldn't want
you to show me

00:26:47.336 --> 00:26:48.496
how that works, would I?

00:26:54.977 --> 00:26:56.672
Hey, kid.

00:26:56.713 --> 00:26:58.271
You were right about one thing.

00:26:58.314 --> 00:27:00.782
I was lying.
I don't eat children.

00:27:00.817 --> 00:27:02.842
You don't scare me.

00:27:02.885 --> 00:27:04.910
My father works
for the Media Bureau.

00:27:04.954 --> 00:27:06.922
And when I tell him
all about this, he'll...

00:27:06.989 --> 00:27:08.854
What is he,
some kind of journalist?

00:27:08.891 --> 00:27:11.325
Yes, and so am I.

00:27:11.360 --> 00:27:13.726
Is that right?

00:27:13.763 --> 00:27:16.095
I report for my school journal.

00:27:16.132 --> 00:27:18.930
That's right where everyone's
going to find out about you

00:27:19.035 --> 00:27:21.629
when I write about this
in next week's edition.

00:27:21.671 --> 00:27:23.036
What's your name?

00:27:23.072 --> 00:27:26.803
- Latika.
- Latika.

00:27:30.880 --> 00:27:31.938
I'm sorry.

00:27:32.048 --> 00:27:34.243
For what?

00:27:38.988 --> 00:27:39.955
I just am.

00:27:39.989 --> 00:27:41.820
I realize how this
must appear to you,

00:27:41.858 --> 00:27:43.257
but I'm just a patriot.

00:27:43.292 --> 00:27:44.418
A patriot?

00:27:44.460 --> 00:27:47.224
I sincerely believe
polaric energy

00:27:47.263 --> 00:27:49.959
has the potential
to destroy this entire world.

00:27:50.032 --> 00:27:52.865
And I take it, very few people
here agree with you?

00:27:52.902 --> 00:27:56.804
We have more support
since the accident at Markov.

00:27:56.839 --> 00:27:59.205
We know the companies
are afraid of us.

00:27:59.242 --> 00:28:02.405
We know they've increased
security at all their plants,

00:28:02.445 --> 00:28:04.936
but it will not be
enough to stop us.

00:28:09.218 --> 00:28:11.243
We can't wait another week.

00:28:11.287 --> 00:28:13.084
We have to move up
the schedule.

00:28:13.122 --> 00:28:15.522
We know they're not telling us
the truth.

00:28:15.558 --> 00:28:18.254
We have to assume
the government sent them.

00:28:18.294 --> 00:28:21.354
Tell everyone
we begin at 0400 tomorrow.

00:28:21.397 --> 00:28:23.797
Wait a minute.

00:28:24.834 --> 00:28:26.529
Captain?

00:28:28.905 --> 00:28:30.270
Kes...

00:28:35.010 --> 00:28:37.274
Do you have something
to tell me, Janeway...

00:28:37.312 --> 00:28:38.643
if that's your real name?

00:28:42.050 --> 00:28:44.314
It is my real name.

00:28:44.352 --> 00:28:46.286
Captain Kathryn Janeway

00:28:46.321 --> 00:28:48.789
of the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:28:54.529 --> 00:28:56.690
I can feel their presence.

00:28:56.731 --> 00:28:58.358
Please elaborate.

00:28:58.400 --> 00:28:59.958
How can you feel their presence?

00:29:00.001 --> 00:29:02.526
I don't know.

00:29:02.570 --> 00:29:04.561
I just can.

00:29:11.546 --> 00:29:13.480
They've been in this room.

00:29:13.515 --> 00:29:15.176
I know it.

00:29:15.216 --> 00:29:18.481
Is there a subspace fracture
anywhere in here?

00:29:18.520 --> 00:29:19.646
Affirmative.

00:29:19.688 --> 00:29:21.178
Set up the equipment.

00:29:26.094 --> 00:29:28.528
You wanted the truth.
All right.

00:29:28.563 --> 00:29:30.588
Here's the truth.

00:29:30.632 --> 00:29:33.100
We're from the future...

00:29:33.134 --> 00:29:36.331
exactly one day in the future.

00:29:36.371 --> 00:29:38.737
You mean I was right?

00:29:38.773 --> 00:29:41.537
We weren't allowed to tell.

00:29:41.576 --> 00:29:43.874
At least, I thought we weren't.

00:29:48.983 --> 00:29:50.848
In a few hours from now,

00:29:50.885 --> 00:29:54.082
there will be a serious accident
on this world.

00:29:54.122 --> 00:29:57.114
It will be caused
by a polaric detonation.

00:29:57.158 --> 00:29:59.319
We came here
in an interstellar ship

00:29:59.361 --> 00:30:01.761
to investigate that explosion.

00:30:01.796 --> 00:30:02.888
When we arrived,

00:30:02.931 --> 00:30:06.367
we were exposed
to the polaric radiation.

00:30:06.401 --> 00:30:11.668
Showing a subspace fracture.
Coordinates: 141 by 21 by 14.

00:30:11.706 --> 00:30:13.640
Five percent drift.
Range: Four meters.

00:30:13.675 --> 00:30:14.733
Got it.

00:30:14.776 --> 00:30:15.834
Initiating generator.

00:30:15.877 --> 00:30:18.368
Initiating microscan
of the subspace fracture.

00:30:19.614 --> 00:30:22.378
It's very likely that whatever
you're planning to do

00:30:22.417 --> 00:30:24.977
could be responsible
for this tragedy.

00:30:25.086 --> 00:30:28.487
And somehow, you were able
to come back here to warn us?

00:30:28.523 --> 00:30:32.357
The explosion had an aftereffect
that no one expected.

00:30:32.394 --> 00:30:35.329
It created fractures in time.

00:30:35.363 --> 00:30:39.094
We fell through
one of those fractures.

00:30:40.735 --> 00:30:43.932
Interstellar ships,
fractures in time...

00:30:43.972 --> 00:30:47.339
do you honestly expect
us to believe all this?

00:30:50.311 --> 00:30:51.642
I found them.

00:30:51.679 --> 00:30:54.307
Scanners are picking up
a subspace beacon.

00:30:54.349 --> 00:30:57.682
Adjusting penetration
coordinates to match.

00:30:57.719 --> 00:31:00.085
I'll try to open up
the other end.

00:31:03.358 --> 00:31:04.882
Chakotay to Janeway.

00:31:04.926 --> 00:31:06.655
Captain, can you read us?

00:31:07.996 --> 00:31:09.190
Eavesdropping devices.

00:31:09.230 --> 00:31:10.197
No,

00:31:10.231 --> 00:31:12.631
but they are for communication.

00:31:12.667 --> 00:31:14.601
My crew is trying
to contact me.

00:31:14.636 --> 00:31:16.604
From the future, of course.

00:31:19.574 --> 00:31:21.599
Get the particle injector.

00:31:27.916 --> 00:31:30.214
Bring them with us...
the boy, too.

00:31:30.251 --> 00:31:31.445
I have an idea
how they can help.

00:31:41.262 --> 00:31:43.127
Chakotay to Janeway.

00:31:43.164 --> 00:31:44.654
Can you read me?

00:31:44.699 --> 00:31:45.961
Please respond.

00:31:53.508 --> 00:31:55.533
I don't get it, Captain.

00:31:55.577 --> 00:31:56.976
This morning
you were giving orders

00:31:57.011 --> 00:31:59.104
about not interfering
because of the Prime Directive.

00:31:59.147 --> 00:32:00.512
Now you're telling them
everything.

00:32:00.548 --> 00:32:02.675
I told them the truth
when I realized

00:32:02.717 --> 00:32:04.685
we'd already violated
the Prime Directive

00:32:04.719 --> 00:32:06.243
in the worst possible manner.

00:32:06.287 --> 00:32:07.914
How did we do that?

00:32:07.956 --> 00:32:09.116
Just by being here.

00:32:09.157 --> 00:32:10.522
Because if we hadn't been here,

00:32:10.558 --> 00:32:13.049
it's very possible this world
would not have been destroyed.

00:32:13.094 --> 00:32:14.425
What?

00:32:14.462 --> 00:32:15.656
Think about it, Tom.

00:32:15.697 --> 00:32:18.257
Before we got involved,
these people were planning

00:32:18.299 --> 00:32:20.460
to commit some kind
of sabotage next week.

00:32:20.502 --> 00:32:23.300
We were the ones who forced
a change in their schedule.

00:32:23.338 --> 00:32:27.206
Because of us, they decided
to begin today at 400 rotations

00:32:27.242 --> 00:32:29.301
and we know the detonation
takes place today

00:32:29.344 --> 00:32:31.209
just after 401.

00:32:31.246 --> 00:32:35.410
401:22:84.

00:32:35.450 --> 00:32:37.315
Wait a minute.

00:32:37.352 --> 00:32:40.378
You're saying we're responsible
for an explosion

00:32:40.421 --> 00:32:42.514
even though it occurred
before our ship arrived here?

00:32:42.557 --> 00:32:44.616
We've traveled back
to a point in time

00:32:44.659 --> 00:32:46.149
before the explosion.

00:32:46.194 --> 00:32:48.788
So, yes, we can be
responsible for it.

00:32:51.799 --> 00:32:56.736
Let's say we never came
and their plans didn't change.

00:32:56.771 --> 00:32:59.467
Wouldn't the accident simply
have occurred next week

00:32:59.507 --> 00:33:00.735
instead of today?

00:33:00.775 --> 00:33:02.936
Who knows what might have
happened between now and then.

00:33:03.044 --> 00:33:04.068
They could have been arrested

00:33:04.112 --> 00:33:05.670
before they got a chance
to carry it out.

00:33:05.713 --> 00:33:06.737
Conditions at the plant

00:33:06.781 --> 00:33:08.612
might not have been
the same next week.

00:33:08.650 --> 00:33:11.619
But it's become
our problem now, Tom,

00:33:11.653 --> 00:33:14.986
and we have got to find
a way to solve it.

00:33:21.529 --> 00:33:22.928
We're running out of time.

00:33:22.964 --> 00:33:24.591
The subspace fractures
are closing.

00:33:24.632 --> 00:33:26.497
We've lost over 70 percent
of them.

00:33:26.534 --> 00:33:28.934
At this point, we're suggesting
we concentrate our search

00:33:28.970 --> 00:33:30.164
at the flash point.

00:33:30.204 --> 00:33:33.264
May I ask what you expect
to accomplish by doing that?

00:33:33.308 --> 00:33:35.674
We figure the Captain and Paris
might have looked

00:33:35.710 --> 00:33:37.803
for the origin of the explosion
to try and prevent it.

00:33:37.845 --> 00:33:38.903
Unlikely.

00:33:38.947 --> 00:33:40.812
It would be a highly
questionable decision

00:33:40.848 --> 00:33:42.315
in light of the Prime Directive.

00:33:42.350 --> 00:33:45.877
If it were me, I would
have tried to get there.

00:33:45.920 --> 00:33:48.946
The issue is whether
Captain Janeway would go there,

00:33:48.990 --> 00:33:50.651
not you, Commander.

00:33:51.960 --> 00:33:53.985
You think you can locate
the flash point?

00:33:54.028 --> 00:33:55.655
We already have.

00:33:57.031 --> 00:33:58.157
Let's go.

00:34:02.437 --> 00:34:04.871
Your job is to get us
past the guards.

00:34:04.906 --> 00:34:06.498
We'll tell them
you're bringing us here

00:34:06.541 --> 00:34:08.566
to negotiate a settlement
of our dispute

00:34:08.610 --> 00:34:09.736
with the power company.

00:34:09.777 --> 00:34:13.543
I cannot and will not
do anything to help you.

00:34:13.581 --> 00:34:15.845
Think before you say no.

00:34:15.883 --> 00:34:17.475
Terla has a weapon
trained on the boy.

00:34:17.518 --> 00:34:19.645
If shooting begins,
he'll be the first victim.

00:34:32.900 --> 00:34:34.299
Is there something
I can do for you?

00:34:34.335 --> 00:34:35.700
She's a government
representative

00:34:35.737 --> 00:34:36.726
on official business.

00:34:47.248 --> 00:34:48.909
I am a hostage.

00:34:48.950 --> 00:34:51.043
These men are here
to break into the plant.

00:35:15.677 --> 00:35:19.408
Their lives are
on your conscience, Janeway!

00:35:22.450 --> 00:35:23.940
You saved my life.

00:35:24.052 --> 00:35:26.850
Don't waste...

00:35:26.888 --> 00:35:29.049
time with me, Captain.

00:35:29.090 --> 00:35:31.422
Got to stop them.

00:35:31.459 --> 00:35:34.792
Will you stay with him
until help arrives?

00:35:34.829 --> 00:35:36.126
Sure he will.

00:35:36.164 --> 00:35:37.461
The kid and I...

00:35:38.499 --> 00:35:40.797
we're old friends now,
aren't we?

00:35:40.835 --> 00:35:41.859
Yeah.

00:35:43.371 --> 00:35:45.202
I'll be back for you.

00:35:49.977 --> 00:35:52.246
We'll be here.

00:36:38.859 --> 00:36:40.588
The polaric levels
are higher here

00:36:40.627 --> 00:36:42.322
than any place
we've been so far.

00:36:42.362 --> 00:36:44.387
This was undoubtedly
the flash point

00:36:44.431 --> 00:36:45.455
of the explosion.

00:36:45.499 --> 00:36:49.458
Whatever went wrong,
it started here.

00:36:49.503 --> 00:36:52.063
Do we have subspace fractures
to work with in here?

00:36:52.105 --> 00:36:53.072
Affirmative.

00:36:53.106 --> 00:36:54.869
They remain quite numerous
in this area.

00:36:54.908 --> 00:36:56.808
Set up the equipment.

00:36:56.843 --> 00:36:58.572
Aye, sir.

00:37:40.587 --> 00:37:42.885
I need the injector.

00:37:45.892 --> 00:37:48.554
Just hand that bag to me.

00:37:53.567 --> 00:37:56.331
41 by 310.

00:37:56.370 --> 00:37:57.701
Two percent drift.

00:37:57.738 --> 00:37:59.171
Range: Six meters.

00:37:59.206 --> 00:38:00.537
Mark.

00:38:00.574 --> 00:38:01.541
I have it.

00:38:01.575 --> 00:38:03.236
Initiating generator.

00:38:03.276 --> 00:38:05.767
Scanning
for the subspace beacon.

00:38:09.416 --> 00:38:11.316
It doesn't look like
they were here.

00:38:11.351 --> 00:38:12.477
It is highly unlikely

00:38:12.519 --> 00:38:14.714
that Captain Janeway
would come here to...

00:38:14.755 --> 00:38:17.781
No, the Captain did come.

00:38:17.824 --> 00:38:19.485
She was here.

00:38:21.261 --> 00:38:23.491
This is where she died.

00:38:25.799 --> 00:38:27.232
Everybody on this planet

00:38:27.267 --> 00:38:29.326
has less
than three minutes to live

00:38:29.369 --> 00:38:31.269
if you go through with this,
Makull.

00:38:31.304 --> 00:38:32.669
Don't!

00:38:33.874 --> 00:38:37.833
What exactly do you think
we are planning to do here?

00:38:37.878 --> 00:38:40.540
I assume you're going
to sabotage the plant

00:38:40.580 --> 00:38:42.946
probably by detonating
some kind of device.

00:38:43.049 --> 00:38:44.949
We're not stupid enough
to blow up anything here.

00:38:45.018 --> 00:38:48.749
That may be true,
but something will go wrong.

00:38:48.789 --> 00:38:50.552
Nothing is going to go wrong

00:38:50.590 --> 00:38:53.957
unless you fire that weapon
near a polaric conduit.

00:38:53.994 --> 00:38:57.623
For everyone's safety,
I suggest you put it down.

00:38:57.664 --> 00:39:00.565
Give me the bag.

00:39:08.508 --> 00:39:12.376
All right, then... we'll wait.

00:39:12.412 --> 00:39:14.403
If Kes is right,
the Captain was here

00:39:14.448 --> 00:39:15.676
at the moment
the explosion occurred.

00:39:15.715 --> 00:39:18.479
Is there any way
to break through subspace

00:39:18.518 --> 00:39:20.452
a few minutes
before the detonation?

00:39:20.487 --> 00:39:21.920
If the widest point
of the fracture

00:39:22.022 --> 00:39:23.580
represents the time
of the explosion,

00:39:23.623 --> 00:39:26.592
couldn't we open a hole
just before the widest point?

00:39:26.626 --> 00:39:28.821
There's no way we could pinpoint
the exact time

00:39:28.862 --> 00:39:32.229
we'd be penetrating, but we
could make an educated guess.

00:39:32.265 --> 00:39:35.291
I feel it is my duty to point
out there is absolutely

00:39:35.335 --> 00:39:37.462
no logical reason
to believe Kes is correct.

00:39:37.504 --> 00:39:42.271
However, since I have no
alternative course of action

00:39:42.309 --> 00:39:44.869
to recommend at this time,
I suggest we proceed.

00:39:44.911 --> 00:39:46.310
Commander?

00:39:52.586 --> 00:39:53.712
What time is it?

00:39:57.390 --> 00:40:00.917
401 rotations plus 21.

00:40:00.961 --> 00:40:05.295
We'll just wait until... 23.

00:40:05.332 --> 00:40:06.856
Twenty-three?

00:40:06.900 --> 00:40:09.425
What's the importance of 23?

00:40:11.838 --> 00:40:13.169
Oh.

00:40:15.509 --> 00:40:18.137
This is all about
the alleged time

00:40:18.178 --> 00:40:20.169
of our self-annihilation.

00:40:20.213 --> 00:40:23.182
All right.

00:40:23.216 --> 00:40:26.185
Let's just see
if we can all get through the...

00:40:28.488 --> 00:40:29.819
What's going on?

00:40:29.856 --> 00:40:32.916
They're cutting
through subspace.

00:40:34.961 --> 00:40:36.792
My God.

00:40:36.830 --> 00:40:41.267
It's going to intersect
with the conduit wall.

00:40:41.301 --> 00:40:43.792
Our own rescue attempt.

00:40:43.837 --> 00:40:45.668
That's what sets it off.

00:40:50.777 --> 00:40:53.371
My weapon may be able
to seal that hole.

00:40:53.413 --> 00:40:55.381
It's our only chance.

00:41:11.731 --> 00:41:13.926
I'm getting nadion particle
resistance from the other side.

00:41:13.967 --> 00:41:17.027
Increasing generator
to maximum output.

00:41:25.011 --> 00:41:27.104
The generator's overloading.

00:41:27.147 --> 00:41:29.172
I don't understand.
It's not working.

00:41:29.215 --> 00:41:31.581
We're not penetrating
the fracture.

00:41:53.707 --> 00:41:56.574
Harry, Harry, Harry,
Harry, Harry.

00:41:56.610 --> 00:41:58.305
You really think
she's going to wait for you?

00:41:58.345 --> 00:41:59.471
I hope so.

00:41:59.512 --> 00:42:01.104
Let her go.

00:42:01.147 --> 00:42:04.139
Let her have a husband
and kids and a good life,

00:42:04.184 --> 00:42:06.448
while you and I have
the Delaney sisters.

00:42:06.486 --> 00:42:09.717
I told you I need to run
a transtator diagnostic.

00:42:09.756 --> 00:42:11.656
You need to run
a self-diagnostic.

00:42:11.691 --> 00:42:13.522
Look, they come as a pair.

00:42:13.560 --> 00:42:15.494
It's a double date or no date.

00:42:15.528 --> 00:42:18.326
Come on.

00:42:18.365 --> 00:42:20.458
I told them all about you.

00:42:20.500 --> 00:42:22.968
What did you tell them
about me?

00:42:23.003 --> 00:42:25.233
Uh, well, for one thing,

00:42:25.271 --> 00:42:27.831
how you broke
the single-pilot speed record

00:42:27.874 --> 00:42:28.966
at the Academy.

00:42:29.009 --> 00:42:30.601
Record?

00:42:30.644 --> 00:42:32.509
I never broke any record.

00:42:32.545 --> 00:42:34.911
And who are they going
to check it with?

00:42:34.948 --> 00:42:36.939
Chakotay to Captain Janeway.

00:42:43.390 --> 00:42:44.721
Yes, Commander.

00:42:44.758 --> 00:42:46.316
We've identified
an M-Class planet

00:42:46.359 --> 00:42:47.986
in the red dwarf system
we're approaching.

00:42:48.094 --> 00:42:50.255
Do you want to change
course to investigate?

00:42:52.232 --> 00:42:54.393
Are you familiar with
any intelligent life-forms

00:42:54.434 --> 00:42:55.662
in this system, Mr. Neelix?

00:42:55.702 --> 00:42:57.135
Familiar?

00:42:57.170 --> 00:43:00.506
Ah, not exactly "familiar."

00:43:00.639 --> 00:43:05.167
Considerably less
than "familiar," actually.

00:43:09.982 --> 00:43:11.506
Kes...

00:43:11.550 --> 00:43:14.075
what are you doing here?

00:43:14.119 --> 00:43:15.381
I had to know.

00:43:15.420 --> 00:43:16.387
Know?

00:43:16.421 --> 00:43:18.218
Know what?

00:43:18.257 --> 00:43:21.954
The planet...
everyone was killed.

00:43:21.994 --> 00:43:24.224
There was this terrible
explosion.

00:43:24.263 --> 00:43:26.493
You, you had a bad dream.

00:43:26.532 --> 00:43:29.626
No. It was more than a dream.

00:43:29.668 --> 00:43:33.399
Mr. Tuvok, any indications
of trouble

00:43:33.438 --> 00:43:34.632
on that M-Class planet?

00:43:34.673 --> 00:43:35.901
Negative, Captain.

00:43:35.941 --> 00:43:37.670
Is it populated?

00:43:37.709 --> 00:43:39.973
Sensors do show humanoid life.

00:43:40.078 --> 00:43:42.706
There is no satellite system

00:43:42.748 --> 00:43:44.978
and no indications
of spacecraft in the vicinity.

00:43:45.083 --> 00:43:47.574
It appears to be
a pre-warp civilization.

00:43:50.188 --> 00:43:51.951
Which means as a policy,

00:43:51.990 --> 00:43:54.151
we don't involve ourselves
in their affairs.

00:43:54.192 --> 00:43:55.887
Of course.

00:43:55.928 --> 00:43:58.328
A most enlightened philosophy.

00:43:58.363 --> 00:43:59.557
Come on, Kes.

00:43:59.598 --> 00:44:01.657
I'm sorry.
Captain...

00:44:01.700 --> 00:44:03.930
Is it possible
to see this planet

00:44:03.969 --> 00:44:05.231
on the viewscreen?

00:44:10.776 --> 00:44:12.175
There it is.

00:44:18.083 --> 00:44:19.550
Thank you.

00:44:24.990 --> 00:44:26.355
Come on.

00:44:28.427 --> 00:44:29.394
Just...

00:44:29.428 --> 00:44:32.886
Enter the planet's
coordinates into the log

00:44:32.931 --> 00:44:34.956
and maintain present heading,
Commander.

00:44:35.000 --> 00:44:37.093
Warp 6.

00:44:37.135 --> 00:44:39.635
Aye, Captain.
